# Interface Concepts for the Open Video Project.

**Authors:** Geisler, Gary, Marchionini, Gary, Nelson, Michael, Spinks, Richard, Yang, Meng

## Abstract
The Open Video Project is an ongoing effort to develop an open source digital video collection that can be used by the information retrieval, digital library, and digital video research communities and ultimately serve a broader audience. Discusses the challenges of compiling and maintaining such a collection. Describes the user interface strategies being developed to enable people to efficiently explore and retrieve video from the collection. (Author/AEF)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ637592

